      },
      "description": "Instructions for correlating metrics, logs, and traces across the observability stack",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "# ChargeRoute Unified Observability Dashboard\n\n## How to Correlate Logs and Traces\n\n1. **From Metrics to Logs**: Click on any service panel → Note the service name → Search in Kibana: `application:\"service-name\"`\n2. **From Logs to Traces**: Find `traceId` field in Kibana logs → Copy trace ID → Paste into Zipkin search\n3. **From Traces to Logs**: Find trace ID in Zipkin → Search in Kibana: `traceId:\"<trace-id>\"`\n4. **Error Investigation**: Check \"Recent Errors\" panel → Click Kibana link → Filter by `level:ERROR` and service name\n5. **Performance Analysis**: Check response time metrics → Find slow traces in Zipkin → Analyze log context in Kibana\n\n**Quick Links**: [Zipkin](http://localhost:9411) | [Kibana](http://localhost:5601) | [Prometheus](http://localhost:9090)",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "10.2.0",
      "title": "Observability Correlation Guide",
      "type": "text"
    },
